{"id": "secure-compilation", "question": "Who studies whether a compiler preserves the guarantees of the source language?", "expected_slugs": ["amal-ahmed"], "expected_sections": ["research_interests", "biography"], "reference": "Amal Ahmed, a professor and associate dean of graduate programs, researches programming languages and compiler verification, focusing on correct and secure compilation, type systems and semantics, gradual typing, software contracts, and safe language interoperability.", "notes": "Paraphrase of 'secure compilation' with no term overlap with the profile."}
